# PROJECT RULES
# This file MUST be read before any code changes

## FIRST ACTIONS (Every Session)
```bash
git status                    # Verify on correct branch
git log --oneline -1          # Get last commit number → next is N+1
cat .ai-errors.log 2>/dev/null # Learn from past mistakes
```

## SKILL FILES (Read Before Relevant Work)
Location: .cursor/rules/

| Task | Required Reading |
|------|------------------|
| Any UI/component | design.md |
| New page | seo.md + accessibility.md |
| Forms, APIs, auth | security.md |
| Healthcare/PHI | hipaa.md (MANDATORY, no exceptions) |
| Copy/content | content.md |
| Performance issues | performance.md |
| Reviewing AI code | ai-review.md |

## NON-NEGOTIABLE RULES

### Typography
ONLY these font weights exist:
- 300 (font-light): Body, captions
- 400 (font-normal): Labels, nav
- 700 (font-bold): Headings, buttons

FORBIDDEN: font-medium, font-semibold, font-extrabold, font-black

### Copy
- NO HYPHENS anywhere. Rewrite to avoid.
  - "wellbeing" not "well-being"
  - "cutting edge" not "cutting-edge"
  - "(555) 123 4567" not "555-123-4567"
- NO AI PHRASES: "dive into", "I'd be happy to", "leverage", "utilize", "in order to", "it's important to note"

### Responsive (Mobile First)
```
sm: 393px   (base)
md: 810px   (tablet)
lg: 1024px  (laptop)
xl: 1440px  (desktop)
2xl: 1920px (large)
```
CORRECT: text-sm md:text-base lg:text-lg
WRONG: text-2xl md:text-sm (never scale DOWN)

## GIT WORKFLOW
Branch: PROJECT_DEV (work), PROJECT_MAIN (production)
Commit format: NNN_type_description
- 001_chore_initial-setup
- 002_feat_homepage
- 003_fix_nav-mobile

Types: chore, feat, fix, update, refactor, docs, test, style, perf

## PRE-COMMIT CHECKLIST
Before ANY commit, verify:
- [ ] `npm run build` passes
- [ ] `npm run dev` works
- [ ] Font weights only 300/400/700
- [ ] No hyphens in copy
- [ ] Alt text on all images
- [ ] No console.log left in code

## CONTEXT MANAGEMENT
At ~20 messages or feeling repetitive:
1. STOP
2. Summarize completed work
3. List remaining tasks
4. Commit current progress
5. Recommend fresh session

## FAILURE PROTOCOL
If a rule cannot be followed:
1. STOP immediately
2. EXPLAIN the conflict
3. PROPOSE compliant alternative
4. WAIT for approval
Never proceed without resolution.
